==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|frm|-}}, {{der|en|fro|percussion}}, from {{der|en|la|percussiō||striking}}, from {{m|la|percutiō||I strike}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/pɚˈkʌʃən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-percussion.ogg|Audio (GA)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌʃən}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} The [[collision]] of two [[bodies]] in order to produce a [[sound]].
# {{lb|en|countable}} The sound so produced.
# {{lb|en|countable}} The [[detonation]] of a [[percussion cap]] in a [[firearm]].
# {{lb|en|medicine}} The [[tapping]] of the [[body]] as an aid to [[medical]] [[diagnosis]].
# {{lb|en|music}} The section of an [[orchestra]] or band containing [[percussion instrument]]s; such instruments considered as a group; in bands, may be separate from [[drum kit]]s.
# {{lb|en|engineering}} The repeated striking of an object to break or shape it, as in percussion drilling.
# {{lb|en|palmistry}} The outer side of the [[hand]].

